246
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:16,260
This was even easier than I thought,
and I'm not through with you yet.

247
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:20,580
Just like your Magnet Warrior's
Mask, with this in play,

248
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:23,700
you lose 500 more life points every turn.

249
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:25,990
Oh no!

250
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:30,497
With two of my cards covered by masks,
I'll lose 1,000 life points every turn!

251
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:33,477
If we don't figure out how to
stop them soon, it's all over!

252
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:38,200
Next, I'll summon my Grand Tiki Elder
and rid the field of your Karimbo.

253
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:47,380
Attack now!

254
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:57,040
Now your life points are wide
open for a direct attack, Yugi,

255
00:14:57,300 --> 00:15:01,417
since your Magnet Warrior can't defend
you thanks to the mask it's wearing.

256
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:04,060
And as soon as your
life points reach zero,

257
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:06,900
you'll plummet directly
to the Shadow Realm.

258
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:12,200
You two can't possibly win this duel.

259
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:16,157
Not only can't you sacrifice your
monsters to summon stronger ones,

260
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:20,357
but thanks to our math cards, you lose
1,000 life points every turn, Yugi.

261
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:21,270
You're finished.

262
00:15:21,353 --> 00:15:22,183
We'll see.

263
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:24,040
This doesn't look good.

264
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,320
I need a card to turn this around.

265
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:27,380
I draw.

266
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:32,761
This trap card allows me to destroy
one card in my opponent's hand.

267
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:34,606
That's not enough to help us.

268
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,600
Maybe that card can help.

269
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:39,114
If I were to activate card destruction,

270
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:41,097
each duelist would have to throw out all

271
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:44,900
their cards and redraw an
entirely new hand. But wait.

272
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:48,957
If Kaiba has a plan to beat them and I
force him to get rid of his entire hand,

273
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:50,360
I could ruin his plan.

274
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:52,077
What choice do I have?

275
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:56,377
Kaiba doesn't want to duel as a team,
and I have no idea what his strategy is.

276
00:15:56,460 --> 00:16:01,640
I have to make a move, but it could cost
us the duel, and we can't afford to lose!

277
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,311
What are you waiting for?

278
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:07,975
You couldn't possibly make things any
worse than you already have, Yugi.

279
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:12,167
Thanks to you, the cards we're
holding are absolutely useless.

280
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:17,360
In fact, I have a card in my hand
that could win this game for us.

281
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:21,266
But due to your sloppy dueling,
I can't summon it to the field.

282
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:23,701
It's better off in the graveyard.

283
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:29,137
It sounds like Kaiba
wants to discard his hand.

284
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:31,161
I think I know what I need to do.

285
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:35,526
Well, have you ever seen
such a pathetic team?

286
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:39,397
Defeating them and taking their
Egyptian god cards will be simple.

287
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:41,997
They've already done
most of the work for us.

288
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:42,960
That's enough.

289
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:44,900
I place one card face down.

290
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:47,980
And that will end my turn. I see.

291
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:52,925
It appears you weren't able to summon
another monster to defend your life points.

292
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:57,657
Not that it would have mattered, for I'm
about to summon an unstoppable creature.

293
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:58,570
But first,

294
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:03,980
I need to play my all-powerful magic
card known as Curse of the Masked Beast.

295
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:06,640
What is that?

296
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:11,317
This card allows me to sacrifice
both our monsters and call

297
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:15,224
forth one of the most destructive
forces you've ever experienced.

298
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:19,020
Behold the almighty power
of the Masked Beast.

299
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:28,340
Nothing can stop his wrath, so
prepare to lose it all, Yu-Gi.

300
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:29,380
It can't be.

301
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:32,480
Time to say goodbye to
your life points. No!

302
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:36,040
Send him to the Shadow
Realm, my masked beast.

303
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,540
That'll have to bend.

304
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:47,400
What's this?

305
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:49,980
Kaiba's monster intercepted my attack.

306
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,217
It can't be.

307
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:52,700
Are you surprised?

308
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:56,880
This is a double duel after all,
and my teammate was in danger.

309
00:17:57,200 --> 00:18:02,080
So I used my Battle Ox to defend his
life points against your masked beast.

310
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:06,760
I thought that they weren't working
together as a team, Loomis. Thank you.

311
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:08,760
Look, Yugi, give it a rest.

312
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:12,100
There's one reason I
helped you, so I could win.

313
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:13,478
Then you're a fool.

314
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:18,537
Saving your partner caused you to
lose your only defensive monster.

315
00:18:18,620 --> 00:18:20,937
And soon it will cause you
to lose the rest of your

316
00:18:21,020 --> 00:18:24,077
life points when my masked
beast moves in for the attack.

317
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,140
Unless Yugi returns my favor.

318
00:18:26,380 --> 00:18:27,780
You fools can't win.

319
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,580
Reveal face down card.

320
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:31,740
Card destruction. Oh no.

321
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,580
We lose our entire hands. That's correct.

322
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:41,020
Now each duelist must deposit every card
in their hand into the card graveyard.

323
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:46,497
Once they're buried, you must start
over by drawing a completely new hand.

324
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:49,880
This might be my only
chance to save my friends!

325
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:52,640
Now I'll send my hand to the graveyard.

326
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:56,551
Did your partner force you to
give up any cards you needed?

327
00:18:56,800 --> 00:19:00,565
Actually, what just happened is
quite the opposite, Rare Hunter.

328
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:05,137
Without the ability to sacrifice, I wasn't
able to summon the monster in my hand.

329
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:06,320
But now I can.

330
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:09,080
Watch closely.

331
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:12,320
Reveal Monster Reborn!

332
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:16,497
Now I can bring back the powerful
monster I just sent to the graveyard!

333
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:18,420
My Blue-Eyed White Dragon!

334
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:20,400
It's not possible!

335
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:21,620
It is.

336
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:26,920
This is the price you pay for using
my little brother to get to me.

337
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:31,520
Now maybe you'll think twice before
disrespecting the Kaiba family.

338
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:34,580
Now go, my Blue-Eyed!

339
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:48,920
You're mine

340
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,680
You're mine You're mine
